Add the lightweight vanilla JS library to keep overall bundle size under the 100KB budget and target an initial load time reduction of 350ms:
```html
<link rel="preload" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/lazysizes/5.3.2/lazysizes.min.js" as="script">
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/lazysizes/5.3.2/lazysizes.min.js" async></script>
```

2. **Markup Structure with Semantic HTML5 Tag Usage Details**:
- Use the semantic `<section id="project-gallery">` tag to define the distinct thematic section for the gallery.
- Structure layout using Bootstrap 5.3.0 grid containers (`container`, `row`, `col-lg-4 col-md-6 col-sm-12`).
- Enclose project cards within standard card markup, using semantic `<h5>` tags for headings, `<p>` for descriptions, and `<img>` tags for images.
- Use `data-src` for the actual image path (optimized to ~180KB, down from 300KB), a low-resolution `src="placeholder.jpg"` to prevent cumulative layout shift, the `card-img-top lazyload` classes, and descriptive `alt` attributes for SEO and accessibility:
```html
<section id="project-gallery">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 col-sm-12 mb-4">
        <div class="card">
          <img data-src="image.jpg" src="placeholder.jpg" class="card-img-top lazyload" alt="Project image description">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h5 class="card-title">Project Title</h5>
            <p class="card-text">Project description.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
```

3. **CSS Styling**:
```css
#project-gallery .card-img-top {
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  object-fit: cover;
}
```

4. **Configuration & Error Handling**:
```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
  const lazyLoadInstance = lazysizes.config({
    loadingClass: 'ls-loading',
    loadedClass: 'ls-loaded',
    lazyClass: 'lazy',
    errorClass: 'ls-error',
  });
  lazyLoadInstance.revalidate();

  document.querySelectorAll('.lazyload').forEach((image) => {
    image.addEventListener('error', () => {
      image.src = 'fallback.jpg';
      image.classList.remove('ls-error');
    });
  });
});
```

